      {
        "id": 125312,
        "name": "Killswitch",
        "username": "Killswitch",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/killswitch/{size}/2116_2.png",
        "created_at": "2015-01-06T00:25:45.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Here's my thought process.</p><p>Backlash Field says:&nbsp;The first time Baron Blade is dealt Damage by a Target each turn<span>, Baron Blade deals that Target 3 Lightning Damage.</span></p><p>Reworded, this card says \"The first time a target deals damage to Baron Blade each turn.\" Each target is independant of one another, so it appears to be a new condition for each one per turn. So the game will check to see if Raptor Bot has dealt BB damage this turn, and react accordingly. It will do the same to Turret Bot, Platform Bot, etc.&nbsp;</p><p>However, moving to Wrong Place and Time, we have:&nbsp;The first time a Hero Target would be dealt Damage each turn<span>, redirect that Damage to Setback, or remove X Tokens from your Unlucky Pool to redirect that Damage to a Target, where X = the amount of Damage.</span></p><p>The wording appears to be the same. Each hero is still independant of each other. The only difference here is they are not dependant on dealing a specific target damage.</p><p>Re-arranging the wording shouldn't matter, should it?</p>",
        "post_number": 25,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T03:59:30.642Z",
